1
00:00:00,944 --> 00:00:03,514
(Hawking:)Sheldon, you're too brilliant.

2
00:00:03,513 --> 00:00:05,613
(Amy:)How can you feel bad

3
00:00:05,615 --> 00:00:07,915
(Amy:)if Stephen Hawking says
you're brilliant?

4
00:00:07,918 --> 00:00:09,618
(Sheldon:)I can't.

5
00:00:09,619 --> 00:00:11,619
(Sheldon:)Thank you, Professor Hawking.

6
00:00:11,621 --> 00:00:13,221
(Sheldon:)You are a gift to mankind.

7
00:00:13,223 --> 00:00:16,153
(Sheldon:)There should be statues
of you everywhere.

8
00:00:16,159 --> 00:00:18,229
(Sheldon:)You know, the Lincoln Memorial
has a big chair.

9
00:00:18,228 --> 00:00:20,058
(Sheldon:)We could swap you right in.

10
00:00:22,332 --> 00:00:26,302
(Hawking:)I always thought a motorized toy
of me would be cool.

11
00:00:29,606 --> 00:00:31,676
What a wonderful idea!

12
00:00:31,675 --> 00:00:34,145
(Sheldon:)How does this man
not have a Nobel?

13
00:00:34,144 --> 00:00:36,144
(Leonard:)Do not tell Wolowitz.
Way ahead of you.

14
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:46,980
(Ellen:)A new study came out,
and it said that laughing

15
00:00:46,986 --> 00:00:49,416
(Ellen:)makes your brain work better.

16
00:00:49,422 --> 00:00:51,222
(Ellen:)And I know that's true
because laughing

17
00:00:51,223 --> 00:00:53,353
has made me the "smartiest."

18
00:00:54,794 --> 00:00:56,094
(Ellen:)Although, on the other hand,

19
00:00:56,095 --> 00:00:57,895
(Ellen:)babies laugh a lot,
and they're dumb.

20
00:00:59,365 --> 00:01:01,195
(Sheldon:)Do people know about her?

21
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:34,010
'Cause she's delightful.

